      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum cascade laser was a conceptually original semiconductor light source that opened major spectral regions to compact, useful coherent radiation.",
        "attribution": "Cho enabled the requisite semiconductor heterostructure technology; Capasso and Faist were central to the invention and demonstration.",
        "maturity": "Its operation, applications, and physical basis have been thoroughly confirmed over decades.",
